The Guild objects to three things in the passage:

- the wide meaning of **specified authority**, which lets agencies beyond the Registrar, possibly even police, carry out the Registrar's functions (option (A));
- the Registrar's power to deny the right to publish and to **cancel registration** under sections 4(1) and 11(4) (option (B));
- Section 6(b), which lets the Registrar or a specified authority **enter the premises** of a periodical to inspect records (option (C)).

Since all three are criticisms the Guild makes, the answer is option (D).
